From 59d2d5aa6818303dc1e984c716e60f3b08065e8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: amittell <mittell@me.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Mar 2026 22:53:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): treat Anthropic long-context usage errors as
 context overflow for compact+retry

Anthropic returns HTTP 429 with the message 'Extra usage is required
for long context requests.' when the session context is too large for
the standard usage tier.  OpenClaw was classifying this as a transient
rate-limit error and cascading through all model fallbacks (which all
fail for the same reason), leaving the user with a hard failure across
every model.

The correct fix is to treat this specific 429 as a context overflow so
it routes to the existing compact+retry path.

Changes:
- Add isAnthropicLongContextUsageError() helper (case-insensitive
  substring match on 'extra usage is required for long context')
- In isLikelyContextOverflowError(), check the new helper *before* the
  isRateLimitErrorMessage() exclusion so the Anthropic long-context
  429 returns true instead of being excluded
- Export the new function from the pi-embedded-helpers barrel
- Add test cases in the existing errors test file
---
